  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\nThe central idea is to transform the minimum overlap problem into a continuous optimization problem using a vectorized representation of the function. We represent the step function as a superposition of basis functions, enabling dimensionality reduction through dimensionality estimation. The optimization proceeds in two phases: global search to explore promising basins and local optimization to converge to locally optimal solutions.\n\nThe key bottleneck of previous approaches is the high dimensionality of the grid-based representation. This approach reduces it by factor of 2-3 while maintaining all relevant interactions. We compute an optimal target dimension based on function complexity and then use bi-level optimization between basis coefficients and sample points. Our algorithm differentiates from previous methods by:\n\n- Adapting dimension dynamically during optimization\n- Using gradient descent on the basis coefficients\n- Maintaining exact integral constraint via design\n- Projecting coefficients to ensure h\u1d62 \u2208 [0,1]\n\n2. Mathematical specifications:\nRepresentation: h(x) = \u03a3\u1d62 \u03b8\u1d62 \u03c6\u1d62(x)\n- \u03c6\u1d62: Basis functions (B-splines) of degree 3\n- \u03b8\u1d62: Coefficients optimized by projected gradient descent\n- Integral constraint: \u222bh(x)dx = \u03a3\u03b8\u1d62 a\u1d62 = 1  \n- Variables: Dimension d \u2208 \u2124\u207a, coefficients \u03b8 \u2208 \u211d\u1d48\n- Objective: min max\u2096\u222bh(x)(1 - h(x+k))dx\n- Constraints: 0 \u2264 \u03b8 \u2208 \u2119\u208a\u1d48 with proper scaling\n\nImplementation: Basis functions defined on [0,2] with periodicity conditions. Conversion between coefficient and sample representations includes boundary extensions and finite differences.\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n    3.1 Dimension selection:\n        - d = ceil(log\u2082(n_points)) \u00d7 \u03c6(overlap_observed)  \n        - \u03c6( ): Scaling factor determined by feature sensitivity\n\n    3.2 Basis function construction:\n        Initialize knots: {\n            t\u2080 = 0, t\u2081 = 1/(d), ..., t\u2096 = 2\n            with spacing corresponding to desired frequency resolution\n        }\n\n    3.3 Projection operator:\n        Project {\u03b8} to feasible space:\n            h_i = B-spline interpolation(\u2211\u03b8\u1d62 \u03c6\u1d62(x))\n            \u03b8 \u2190 \u03a0{ [0,1] } via Legendre projection\n\n    3.4 Optimization loop:\n        while time_remaining > 10s:\n            Compute gradients using AD:\n                \u2207f(\u03b8) = \u03a3\u208d\u2096\u208e [\u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx \u00b7 \u2207h(\u03b8)]\n            Projected gradient descent:\n                \u03b8 \u2190 \u03a0(\u03b8 - \u03b1 \u2207f(\u03b8))\n            Update d based on convergence rate\n\n    4. Search choices:\n        - Initial dimension d0: 128\n        - \u03b1 \u2208 [1e-4, 5e-3] (learning rate)\n        - Schedule: Decrease learning rate exponentially with warmup\n        - Check restarts every 1000 iterations if gradient norm < 1e-3\n\n    5. Budget allocation:\n        - Priming time: 30s for initial dimension scan\n        - Main optimization: 50% time budget\n        - Dimension adjustment: 20% budget for switching d\n        - Validation time: 10% budget for reprojection\n\n    6. Error handling:\n        - Dimension trapping if d<64: revert to d0\n        - NaN values: Fall back to gradient-free optimization\n        - Infeasible projections: Apply dimension expansion\n\n4. Mathematical guarantees:\n    For the dimension choice: d \u2265 c\u00b7log(1/\u03b5) ensures |error| \u2264 \u03b5\n    Gradients computed via:\n        \u2207\u2095\u1eac = \u222b (1 - h_bar(x+k)) \u00b7 \u03b4_k (x - x\u2c7c) dx\n        where \u03b4_k/denotes distribution implementataion oversight\n\n5. Restart mechanisms:\n    Store best candidates every 50 iterations. If plateau detected over 500 iterations, restart from best candidate with dimension increased by 25%\n\n6. Dimension switching:\n    Toggle dimension when: \n        (1) Current dimension > median(feature_scales)\n        (2) Temporal variance in f-values > threshold\n    d_new = current_d \u00d7 1.5 floor to power of 2\n\n7. Validation checks:\n    Final verification:\n        |\u222bh(x)dx - 1| < 1e-6\n        max|\u2207h(x)| < 1.0/d\n        for all i s.t. h[i]\u2209[0,1] reproject\n    Implement restart if constraints violated\n\n8. Fallback:\n    If time_\u03d5 = 0: \n        h \u2190 initial_h_values\n        project_feasible(h, 1)\n        compute_c5(h)\n    Reserve 30 seconds for fallback if search stalls",
